    {
        "content": "<div class=\"codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code>Cell := { text : Str }.{\n    is_eq : _\n}\n\nRow := [Header(List(Cell)), Data(List(Cell))].{\n    is_eq : _\n}\n\nmain! = |_args| {\n    header_a = Header([{ text: \"a\" }])\n\n    header_b = Header([{ text: \"b\" }])\n\n    data_a = Data([{ text: \"a\" }])\n\n    dbg header_a.is_eq(header_a)\n    dbg header_a.is_eq(header_b)\n    dbg header_a.is_eq(data_a)\n    dbg data_a.is_eq(data_a)\n\n    Ok({})\n}\n</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code>$ roc example.roc\n[dbg] True\n[dbg] False\n[dbg] False\n[dbg] True\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 625376612,
        "sender_full_name": "Luke Boswell",
        "timestamp": 1789787378
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"341568\">Jared Ramirez</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/231634-beginners/topic/match.20multiple.20variants/near/625352546\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I think you need to wrap it in a tuple</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>yeah, that's the issue - it's a syntax problem, not related to <code>is_eq</code>.</p>",
        "id": 625377932,
